    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d312">

                <pb facs="0449" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1945v05/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/1–1345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Portugal</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-13T20:00:00-04:00">January 13, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>82. The War Department desires to obtain the permission of the Portuguese
                    Government to make landings in Lisbon of planes of the Air Transport Command on
                    regularly scheduled flights from the United States to Paris and Rome. As Mr.
                        George<anchor n="1" xml:id="d312-f1"/> is thoroughly familiar with this
                    project he is being sent to Lisbon, accompanied by Colonel Payne,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d312-f2"/> to assist you. They expect to leave Washington the
                    morning of the 16th by transport plane and to proceed via Casablanca.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d312-f1" n="1" xml:id="d312-f1-content">
                <p>William Perry George, Assistant Chief of the Division of Western European
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d312-f2" n="2" xml:id="d312-f2-content">
                <p>Lt. Col. Robert G. Payne of the Air Transport Command.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
